{"name":"Sargasso Sea","hex":"#3d4a67","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sargasso Sea","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An elongated area in the middle of the North Atlantic Ocean, surrounded by ocean currents."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sargasso_Sea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sargasso Sea","blocks":[{"text":"The Sargasso Sea is a region of the Atlantic Ocean bounded by four currents forming an ocean gyre. It is the only named sea without land boundaries. It is distinguished from other parts of the Atlantic Ocean by its characteristic brown Sargassum seaweed and calm blue waters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Sargasso_2.svg/330px-Sargasso_2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sargasso_Sea","wikidata":"Q169274"},{"title":"Sargasso Sea (Pram album)","blocks":[{"text":"Sargasso Sea is an album by the English band Pram, released in 1995."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d8/Pram_-_Sargasso_Sea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sargasso_Sea_(Pram_album)","wikidata":"Q7423897"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/North_Atlantic_Gyre.png/50